# P6: LeakSanitizer suppressions for the tiles_renderer test suite.
#
# Policy (docs/adr/0007-sanitizer-memory-robustness.md):
#   - Leaks in OUR code (src/, samples/) are BUGS: fix them, never suppress.
#   - Entries below are third-party one-time-initialization / driver leaks
#     (Mesa, X11, SDL, Filament prebuilts, cesium-native) that we cannot fix.
#   - Every entry MUST carry a comment naming the source and the evidence
#     (which scenario reported it). Overly broad patterns (e.g. "leak:libGL*")
#     are banned: they would hide real Filament/GL resource leaks, which are
#     our responsibility to destroy (see Renderer::shutdown ordering).
#
# Format: one "leak:<substring>" per line, matched against the allocation
# stack. See https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer
#
# (Populated from real triage runs; empty until the first report is
# classified.)

# --- Entry 1 (2026-09-29): cesium-native CurlAssetAccessor handle-cache leak.
# Source: cesium-native v0.64.0, CesiumCurl/src/CurlAssetAccessor.cpp.
#   struct CurlAssetAccessor::CurlCache keeps a std::vector of CURL* handles
#   (curl_easy_init'ed in get(), reset in release()) but defines NO
#   destructor, and ~CurlAssetAccessor() only calls curl_global_cleanup() —
#   grep confirms zero curl_easy_cleanup() calls in the file. Every cached
#   handle (plus its 3 MiB transfer buffer from Curl_multi_xfer_buf_borrow,
#   connection/SSL-session/DNS state) leaks when the accessor is destroyed.
# Evidence: sanitizer_http (HTTP tileset via local http.server) reported
#   9.4 MiB in 102 allocations, all with libcurl-internal top frames
#   (Curl_multi_xfer_buf_borrow, Curl_open, Curl_multi_handle,
#   Curl_ssl_scache_create, ...). Our code never calls libcurl directly; in
#   this binary curl is reachable only through CesiumCurl, so matching
#   curl-internal symbols cannot hide one of our own leaks.
# Proper fix (upstream): give CurlCache a destructor that calls
#   curl_easy_cleanup() on every cached handle.
leak:Curl_
leak:curlx_
leak:ip2addr
leak:parseurl_and_replace
